ensation","l":"Share-based Payment Arrangement, Noncash Expense","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"rev_contract":{"c":"us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax","l":"Revenue from Contract with Customer, Excluding Assessed Tax","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"capex":{"c":"us-gaap:PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment","l":"Payments to Acquire Property, Plant, and Equipment","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"}},"lines_struct":null,"lines":null,"lines_py":null,"notes":{}}},"intro":{"text":"GEN Korean BBQ (Nasdaq: GENK) is one of the largest Asian casual dining restaurant concepts in the United States. Founded in 2011 by two Korean immigrants in Los Angeles, the brand has now grown to 54 company-owned locations where guests serve as their own chefs, preparing meals on embedded grills in the center of each table. The extensive menu consists of traditional Korean and Korean-American food, including high-quality meats, poultry, seafood and mixed vegetables. With its unique culinary experience alongside its modern d\u00e9cor and lively atmosphere, GEN Korean BBQ delivers an engaging and interactive dining experience that appeals to a vast segment of the population. Beyond the restaurants, GEN is building a rapidly growing retail business, bringing its signature Korean BBQ flavors to grocery and warehouse club retailers nationwide.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1891856/000119312526342377/genk-ex99_1.htm","filed":"2026-08-10","source":"8-K"},"da_v":2}